# Frontend Rules

- Build mobile, tablet, laptop, desktop, and wide-desktop experiences.
- Use semantic HTML and accessible controls.
- Reuse the design system.
- Keep business logic out of presentational components where practical.
- Keep mock data behind a data-access boundary.
- Do not directly couple UI components to database internals.
- Product listing must support category-aware filters.
- Technical specifications must remain readable and structured.
- Product cards must communicate product, price, availability, warranty, and key actions clearly.
- Avoid visual clutter, excessive gradients, excessive glassmorphism, and unnecessary animation.
- Preserve fast route transitions and small client bundles.
